EXTERNAL flag(name)
Two ravens are sitting on your table when you arrive, one at each end, like bookends that don't like each other.
"Huginn and Muninn," says Skögul. "Thought and Memory. Odin's." # speaker: skogul
"Until now Huginn's done the talking: how they died. From today Muninn talks too. He remembers how they lived. Oaths kept and broken, which god they prayed to, whose sword it was." # speaker: skogul
"They never lie. They might seem to disagree. Huginn says a man died with his axe in his hand; Muninn says he broke his oath on the ring. Both true. The Order of Judgment says which one counts." # speaker: skogul
Muninn clears his throat, which is a horrible sound in a raven.
"And Muninn forgets. More every day now. Odin says he fears Huginn won't come back to him, but he fears more for Muninn." # speaker: skogul
* ["Why is he forgetting?"]
  "Because the end is coming, and memory goes first." # speaker: skogul
  She doesn't look at the raven when she says it. The raven looks at her.
* ["Which one do I trust?"]
  "Both. Always both. Then open the book." # speaker: skogul
- Huginn hops down the table to the first soul in the queue and starts telling you, very fast, about a spear.
{ flag("loki_in_valhalla"):
  "One more thing," says Skögul, without looking up. "The man with the scarred lips has a seat on Odin's benches now. The einherjar have started fighting before breakfast, and nobody can say who started it." # speaker: skogul
}
